      "label": "Dyslexia Stereotype",
      "description": "A harmful stereotype that falsely implies people with dyslexia are less capable of understanding consent or are more likely to be sexually available, often used in a derogatory or mocking manner. This stereotype is rooted in ableist assumptions and misrepresents the cognitive abilities of individuals with dyslexia.",
